              "text": "You can download the latest version of Python directly from the official website:\n\n**[Official Python Downloads Page](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**\n\n### Current Version Information\nAs of mid-2026, the latest stable series is **Python 3.14** (specifically version **3.14.5**), while **Python 3.13** remains a highly supported stable release. \n\n### How to Install for Your Operating System:\n* **Windows:** The main download page will automatically detect your OS and offer an installer. You can also download it from the **Microsoft Store** (by searching for Python) for a simplified, sandboxed installation.\n* **macOS:** You can download the `.pkg` installer directly from the Python website, or install and manage it using a package manager like **Homebrew** (`brew install python`).\n* **Linux/UNIX:** Most modern Linux distributions come with Python pre-installed. If you need the latest version, you can typically update it using your system's package manager (such as `apt` for Ubuntu/Debian, `dnf` for Fedora, or `pacman` for Arch Linux), or build it from the official source code.",
